      {
        "id": 2651196570,
        "content": "In all other apps, the button is placed onto a container that has darker color for example:\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5c828de1-c7d0-483c-8f73-83909d7ff485)\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/02e3458e-ba87-421e-a21d-0e3a4166fe1d)\r\nSo this is the first case I saw where the button is placed directly on the background, but it seems that it's too transparent only on my monitor. \r\nI agree, we should make a library with our UI components so that all projects can import it.\r\nIt also works fine for me on work.ubq.fi. It might be because it's running locally but not sure\r\nI dig deeper into this and it seems that the Supabase Github tokens get stored in the local storage with a key that reflects the project id for example the key is `sb-wfzpewmlyiozupulbuur-auth-token` where `wfzpewmlyiozupulbuur` is the project id, so if the project id changes for example when running locally, it won't work.\r\nThis might also be the reason why login doesn't persist when running locally with a different project.",
